{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cesh7tm9qeY1YkTdYn9Vk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! The implementation is complete. Here's a summary of what was implemented:\n\n## Summary of Changes\n\nI've successfully implemented the order cancellation feature with the following changes:\n\n### 1. **Order Entity** (`Order.kt`)\n- Added `OrderStatus` enum with `ACTIVE` and `CANCELLED` states\n- Added `status` field to Order with default value `ACTIVE`\n\n### 2. **API Error Codes** (`ApiError.kt`)\n- Added `ORDER_CANCELLED` - for 409 when creating shipment for cancelled order\n- Added `CANNOT_CANCEL_ORDER_WITH_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT` - for 409 when cancelling order with confirmed shipment\n\n### 3. **Shipment Repository** (`ShipmentRepository.kt`)\n- Added `findByOrderId()` method to query shipments by order ID\n\n### 4. **Order Controller** (`OrderController.kt`)\n- Added `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint with the following logic:\n  - Returns 404 if order doesn't exist\n  - Returns success without changes if already `CANCELLED` (supports idempotent retries)\n  - Rejects with 409 if any shipment is `CONFIRMED` (nothing changes)\n  - Otherwise: cancels the order and all its `CREATED` shipments\n\n### 5. **Shipment Controller** (`ShipmentController.kt`)\n- Added validation to prevent creating shipments for cancelled orders (409 with `ORDER_CANCELLED`)\n- Maintains existing behavior for non-existent orders\n\n## Verification\n✅ All 13 existing tests pass\n✅ No new dependencies added\n✅ Only order, shipment, and api package files modified\n✅ All acceptance criteria met"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":360,"cache_read_input_tokens":51052,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":360},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_av